  "note": "Third remediation revision (findings F1-F9 from an independent static review, validated by a second agent). Applied to BOTH the private bench copy and this portable copy: parser containment and bounded/sanitised diagnostics, the reporter-to-collector null contract, a control-master liveness gate with no interactive fallback, recorded tri-state ownership with durable pending-cleanup evidence, SIGHUP/SIGTERM teardown in both modes, verified master shutdown, explicit boot identity, and reporter output-integrity/format fixes. Only deliberate configuration differences remain (bench target/user, data dir, artifact and known_hosts defaults and pinned digests, and config.example.json). The two trees' collector tests are now byte-identical, so no sanitized test addresses remain. Second follow-up (collector 1.5.2): provisioning facts are read where a failed start() enters the collector, so no classifier branch can drop them; a cancellation during the control-master exit is held for one bounded check, recorded by stage and re-raised. Every hash below was regenerated from the files themselves in that revision: eight portable entries had not been refreshed for 1.5.1 and no longer matched the committed files, and the two follow-up regression suites were not listed.",
